# Files a fresh worktree must carry that .gitignore keeps out of git.
#
# `git worktree add` checks out TRACKED files only, so an agent in a worktree starts with no fonts, no
# scenes, and no bin/vawe — and the failure is quiet rather than loud. A gate that walks the library
# finds 41 scenes instead of 149 and reports a confident green, which is the exact shape of every gate
# bug logged this week.
#
# Kept SMALL on purpose. The heavy directories are handled by scripts/dev/worktree.sh instead:
# node_modules (106M) and site/node_modules (338M) are shared read-only, and .venv-tools (457M) and
# refs/ (27M) are not needed to run a gate. Copying half a gigabyte per agent is the cost that makes
# people abandon worktrees.

# Licensed faces. Without these the engine substitutes silently and every render is subtly wrong.
assets/fonts/local/**
# THE VENDORED WEBFONTS TOO. `assets/fonts/*.woff2` is gitignored (make fonts downloads it), and this
# file listed only `local/**`, so an agent in a fresh worktree rendered EVERY scene in a fallback serif
# and nothing said so. It found the defect by reading its own contact sheet and mistaking it for a copy
# problem. That is the silent-substitution class this repo logs most, wearing the worktree's clothes.
assets/fonts/*.woff2

# The scene library. 108 of 149 scenes are gitignored, so without this a worktree cannot gate the
# library at all — and says so by finding nothing.
formats/scene/*.json

# Captured product UI. A missing capture renders a grey placeholder box, not an error.
assets/brands/**/components/*.json
assets/brands/**/scenes/*.json

# BRAND IMAGES. `assets/brands/**` is gitignored (captured product UI and marks, per-brand), and 142 of
# the 196 local image paths the scene library references live there. A worktree without them used to
# render holes; since core/boot.js started REFUSING a missing repo-local asset, it stops the boot
# instead — so ~20 scenes became un-runnable in every worktree the moment that refusal landed.
#
# The refusal is right (a missing local asset IS invalid input, and rendering a hole is the silent
# substitution this repo logs most). What was wrong is that the worktree never carried the files. This
# is the same lesson as the fonts line above, one directory over: a fresh worktree that cannot see what
# main sees does not find bugs, it invents them.
assets/brands/**
assets/cutouts/**

# THEMES. `themes/*.json` is partly gitignored (35 ship, more sit on a working machine), and a scene
# naming one that is absent does not degrade — `core/boot.js` refuses to boot at all: `theme "stripe"
# not found (themes/stripe.json) — no default look exists`. A worktree without them cannot render the
# library it was just handed, which is the failure this whole file exists to prevent.
themes/*.json

# Generated art the scene library references (assets/gen is gitignored, like every other produced file).
assets/gen/**

# AUDIO ANALYSIS SIDECARS. `assets/music/**` is gitignored, and a scene with an audio-reactive track
# reads its precomputed spectrum from here. Without it the track DEGRADES SILENTLY — it renders, it
# just reacts to nothing — which is how one scene (react-demo) appeared to render differently in every
# worktree for a whole session. Four agents investigated it; none found the missing file, because
# nothing in the output pointed at audio. docs/MISTAKES.md #465.
assets/music/*.json
